- Write miss performs BusRdX → full-line LLC read → replace one 64-bit word → install M/dirty.
- Coherence controller serializes requests with round-robin arbitration and queries other caches in parallel.
- Controller remains locked until the requester reports its final line installation.
- Query FSM is independent and has priority over local cache commits.
- LLC ownership uses NOT_IN_USE, MAIN_FSM, and COH_FSM; coherence wins simultaneous acquisition but cannot
  preempt an active AXI transaction.

- Both FSMs submit a generic cache_update_t bundle through one cache write port.
- An external query locks its direct-mapped index until writeback and MESI update finish.
- New upstream accesses to that index are backpressured.
- Already accepted conflicting requests retain their request registers and replay lookup after unlock.
- No separate snoop judger is required; the query FSM can generate the external update bundle directly.
